#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking bread was flat and baked on hot stones; honey made it a treat."
msgstr ""
"Das Brot der Wikinger war flach und wurde auf heißen Steinen gebacken; mit Honig wurde es ein "
"Leckerbissen."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Chieftain's Feast"
msgstr "Das Fest des Häuptlings"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My daughter Thora turns twelve! A feast with the whole valley: bring me three crates of mead and "
"two of cheese, within three days."
msgstr ""
"Meine Tochter Thora wird zwölf! Ein Fest mit dem ganzen Tal: {crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} mir drei "
"Kisten Met und zwei Kisten Käse, innerhalb von drei Tagen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The mead! The skalds will sing."
msgstr "Der Met! Die Skalden werden singen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cheese, mead, songs and a fire! Come in, sit by me: it is the best birthday ever."
msgstr ""
"Käse, Met, Lieder und ein Feuer! {crew|Komm|Komm|Kommt} herein, {crew|setz dich|setz dich|setzt "
"euch} zu mir: Das ist der schönste Geburtstag überhaupt."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A chieftain's hall had a long fire in the middle, and benches along the walls."
msgstr ""
"In der Halle eines Häuptlings brannte in der Mitte ein langes Feuer, und an den Wänden standen "
"Bänke."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Ferryman's Tale"
msgstr "Die Geschichte des Fährmanns"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Old Halvard told a story here last night: a hidden cove, where the swans of the lakes are born. He"
" says: ask the potter, the miller and the old man of Svanetorp."
msgstr ""
"Der alte Halvard hat gestern Abend hier eine Geschichte erzählt: von einer versteckten Bucht, wo "
"die Schwäne der Seen geboren werden. Er sagt: {crew|Frag|Frag|Fragt} die Töpferin, die Müllerin "
"und den alten Mann aus Svanetorp."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The cove? My grandmother said: it lies where the reeds grow tallest. Ask Astrid."
msgstr ""
"Die Bucht? Meine Großmutter sagte: Sie liegt dort, wo das Schilf am höchsten wächst. "
"{crew|Frag|Frag|Fragt} Astrid."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Reeds? The tallest ones grow south, by Svanetorp. Go to Grim."
msgstr "Schilf? Das höchste wächst im Süden, bei Svanetorp. {crew|Geh|Geh|Geht} zu Grim."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"So you found my secret. Behind my farm, in the reeds: the swan cove. Look, the cygnets! Grey and "
"fluffy. Tell no one!"
msgstr ""
"{crew|Du hast|Du hast|Ihr habt} also mein Geheimnis gefunden. Hinter meinem Hof, im Schilf: die "
"Schwanenbucht. {crew|Schau|Schau|Schaut}, die Jungen! Grau und flauschig. "
"{crew|Verrate|Verrate|Verratet} es niemandem!"

#. a gift for a task: 'You get ...'
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "the secret of the swan cove"
msgstr "das Geheimnis der Schwanenbucht"

#. the thing 'the secret of the swan cove' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the
#. direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain
#. translation
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "the secret of the swan cove"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Young swans are grey, not white; they are called cygnets."
msgstr "Junge Schwäne sind grau, nicht weiß; man nennt sie Schwanenküken."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Wool for the Winter Cloth"
msgstr "Wolle für den Winterstoff"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Everybody wants warm cloth for the winter, and my looms are hungry. Bring me four crates of wool, "
"and I give you a bolt of red cloth."
msgstr ""
"Alle wollen warmen Stoff für den Winter, und meine Webstühle sind hungrig. "
"{crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} mir vier Kisten Wolle, dann gebe ich {crew|dir|dir|euch} einen Ballen "
"roten Stoff."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Clack, clack, goes the loom. Here: the reddest cloth I ever made, for you."
msgstr ""
"Klack, klack, macht der Webstuhl. Hier: der röteste Stoff, den ich je gemacht habe, für "
"{crew|dich|dich|euch}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The women of a viking farm wove all the cloth: sails, clothes and blankets."
msgstr "Auf einem Wikingerhof webten die Frauen den ganzen Stoff: Segel, Kleider und Decken."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flax in the Field"
msgstr "Flachs auf dem Feld"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Linen is softer than wool on the skin. Plant flax on your farm! When it blooms blue and is ripe, "
"bring me two crates."
msgstr ""
"Leinen ist auf der Haut weicher als Wolle. {crew|Pflanze|Pflanze|Pflanzt} Flachs auf "
"{crew|deinem|deinem|eurem} Hof! Wenn er blau blüht und reif ist, {crew|bring|bring|bringt} mir "
"zwei Kisten."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flax seed in the field. In a few days, it blooms blue."
msgstr "Flachssamen auf dem Feld. In ein paar Tagen blüht er blau."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Your own flax! I will make you linen shirts, soft as a cloud."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Dein|Dein|Euer} eigener Flachs! Ich mache {crew|dir|dir|euch} Leinenhemden, weich wie eine "
"Wolke."

#. a gift for a task: 'You get ...'
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "linen shirts"
msgstr "Leinenhemden"

#. the thing 'linen shirts' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the direct object),
#. e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "linen shirts"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flax was soaked, beaten and combed for weeks before it could be spun into linen."
msgstr ""
"Flachs wurde wochenlang eingeweicht, geschlagen und gekämmt, bevor man ihn zu Leinen spinnen "
"konnte."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Barley for the Brewer"
msgstr "Gerste für den Brauer"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Orm of Hallvik wants the biggest barrel of ale for the autumn feast. I need grain, five crates! "
"Bring them, and you get two crates of my ale."
msgstr ""
"Orm aus Hallvik will das größte Fass Bier für das Herbstfest. Ich brauche Getreide, fünf Kisten! "
"{crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} sie mir, dann {crew|bekommst du|bekommst du|bekommt ihr} zwei Kisten von"
" meinem Bier."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Into the water with it, let it sprout... In a week, the best ale of the lakes!"
msgstr "Ab ins Wasser damit, damit es keimt ... In einer Woche gibt es das beste Bier auf den Seen!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ale was brewed from barley and water, often with herbs instead of hops."
msgstr "Bier braute man aus Gerste und Wasser, oft mit Kräutern statt Hopfen."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Proper Hold"
msgstr "Ein richtiger Laderaum"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You are real traders now: you need a real hold! Bring me eight planks from Frosttorp and two "
"crates of iron tools, and pay 20 silver. Then your hold takes two more crates."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Du bist|Du bist|Ihr seid} jetzt {crew|ein echter Händler|eine echte Händlerin|echte "
"Händler|echte Händlerinnen}: {crew|Du brauchst|Du brauchst|Ihr braucht} einen richtigen Laderaum! "
"{crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} mir acht Planken aus Frosttorp und zwei Kisten Eisenwerkzeug, und "
"{crew|zahl|zahl|zahlt} 20 Silber. Dann fasst {crew|dein|dein|euer} Laderaum zwei Kisten mehr."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Planks of pine, split with wedges. Stack them well!"
msgstr "Kiefernplanken, mit Keilen gespalten. {crew|Staple|Staple|Stapelt} sie gut!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Good iron! Now my wages."
msgstr "Gutes Eisen! Jetzt meinen Lohn."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Saw, plane, rivets... Look at her! Longer, wider, and room for two more crates."
msgstr ""
"Säge, Hobel, Nieten ... {crew|Schau es dir an|Schau es dir an|Schaut es euch an}! Länger, breiter,"
" und Platz für zwei Kisten mehr."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Plank"
msgstr "Planke"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a plank|{count} planks}"
msgstr "{count|eine Planke|{count} Planken}"

#. the thing '{count|a plank|{count} planks}' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative
#. (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the
#. plain translation
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a plank|{count} planks}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking boats were built of overlapping planks, held with iron rivets."
msgstr ""
"Wikingerboote baute man aus Planken, die sich überlappten und mit Eisennieten gehalten wurden."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Messenger's Cold"
msgstr "Die erkältete Botin"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Atchoo! I have a cold, and I must tell the smith, the horse farm and the herders about the autumn "
"feast at Hallvik. Can you do it today? Atchoo!"
msgstr ""
"Hatschi! Ich bin erkältet, und ich muss dem Schmied, dem Pferdehof und den Hirten vom Herbstfest "
"in Hallvik erzählen. {crew|Kannst du|Kannst du|Könnt ihr} das heute machen? Hatschi!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The autumn feast? I will bring my best knives to show."
msgstr "Das Herbstfest? Ich bringe meine besten Messer mit, zum Zeigen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "We will come with all the horses! Tell Inga to drink hot honey water."
msgstr ""
"Wir kommen mit allen Pferden! {crew|Sag|Sag|Sagt} Inga, sie soll heißes Honigwasser trinken."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A feast! I will bring my flute. Thank you!"
msgstr "Ein Fest! Ich bringe meine Flöte mit. Danke!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Messengers rowed, rode and ran: news could cross a land in a few days."
msgstr ""
"Boten ruderten, ritten und rannten: Neuigkeiten konnten in wenigen Tagen ein ganzes Land "
"durchqueren."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hay for Frosttorp"
msgstr "Heu für Frosttorp"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My hay meadow was flooded, and the cows are hungry! I need eight crates of hay. Your big boat can "
"do it in one trip."
msgstr ""
"Meine Heuwiese wurde überschwemmt, und die Kühe haben Hunger! Ich brauche acht Kisten Heu. "
"{crew|Dein|Dein|Euer} großes Boot schafft das in einer Fahrt."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Moo! Listen to them, they are happy. You saved my winter. Take this cheese."
msgstr ""
"Muh! {crew|Hör|Hör|Hört} nur, sie sind glücklich. {crew|Du hast|Du hast|Ihr habt} meinen Winter "
"gerettet. {crew|Nimm|Nimm|Nehmt} diesen Käse."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hay is dried grass; without enough of it, a farm could not keep its animals over winter."
msgstr ""
"Heu ist getrocknetes Gras; ohne genug davon konnte ein Hof seine Tiere nicht über den Winter "
"bringen."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sigvor's Cheese"
msgstr "Sigvors Käse"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My goats gave so much milk this summer! I made four big wheels of cheese for Orm's autumn feast in"
" Hallvik, but my boat is full of goats. Will you carry them?"
msgstr ""
"Meine Ziegen haben diesen Sommer so viel Milch gegeben! Ich habe vier große Laibe Käse für Orms "
"Herbstfest in Hallvik gemacht, aber mein Boot ist voller Ziegen. {crew|Bringst du|Bringst "
"du|Bringt ihr} sie hin?"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sigvor's cheese! The guests will fight over it. Well, not fight: they will ask nicely."
msgstr ""
"Sigvors Käse! Die Gäste werden sich darum streiten. Na ja, nicht streiten: Sie werden nett fragen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Roll them in gently. And no nibbling!"
msgstr "{crew|Roll|Roll|Rollt} sie vorsichtig hinein. Und nicht naschen!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cheese"
msgstr "Käse"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a wheel of cheese|{count} wheels of cheese}"
msgstr "{count|ein Laib Käse|{count} Laibe Käse}"

#. the thing '{count|a wheel of cheese|{count} wheels of cheese}' for {thing@acc} in the
#. translations: the accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty
#. if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a wheel of cheese|{count} wheels of cheese}"
msgstr "{count|einen Laib Käse|{count} Laibe Käse}"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cheese keeps the milk of the summer for the winter."
msgstr "Käse hebt die Milch des Sommers für den Winter auf."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Cow of Our Own"
msgstr "Eine eigene Kuh"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With the east meadow, we have room for a cow at last! Buy one at the horse farm in Torsgården. A "
"cow is big, but she fits in your boat like a crate, if she stands still."
msgstr ""
"Mit der Ostwiese haben wir endlich Platz für eine Kuh! {crew|Kauf|Kauf|Kauft} eine auf dem "
"Pferdehof in Torsgården. Eine Kuh ist groß, aber sie passt in {crew|dein|dein|euer} Boot wie eine "
"Kiste, wenn sie still steht."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Look at her big brown eyes! She will give us milk every day. Let us call her Rosa."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Schau|Schau|Schaut} nur ihre großen braunen Augen an! Sie gibt uns jeden Tag Milch. Wir "
"nennen sie Rosa."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/042_a_cow_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cows were the wealth of a farm: a family counted its riches in cows."
msgstr "Kühe waren der Reichtum eines Hofes: Eine Familie zählte ihren Reichtum in Kühen."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pots for Ekvik"
msgstr "Töpfe für Ekvik"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The fish soup! We cook it for the whole village, but our big pot cracked. Bring us three crates of"
" pots from the potter, please."
msgstr ""
"Die Fischsuppe! Wir kochen sie für das ganze Dorf, aber unser großer Topf hat einen Sprung. "
"{crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} uns bitte drei Kisten Töpfe von der Töpferin."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "New pots! Tonight there is fish soup for everybody, and for you two the first bowl."
msgstr ""
"Neue Töpfe! Heute Abend gibt es Fischsuppe für alle, und {crew|für dich|für dich|für euch zwei} "
"die erste Schale."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/043_pots_for_ekvik/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The cooking pot hung over the fire on a chain, and the soup simmered all day."
msgstr "Der Kochtopf hing an einer Kette über dem Feuer, und die Suppe köchelte den ganzen Tag."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ragna's Broken Oar"
msgstr "Ragnas zerbrochenes Ruder"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Ragna rowed out at dawn and is not back! I fear her oar broke. Find her on the lakes, then come "
"back and fetch the spare oar for her."
msgstr ""
"Ragna ist im Morgengrauen hinausgerudert und noch nicht zurück! Ich fürchte, ihr Ruder ist "
"zerbrochen. {crew|Such|Such|Sucht} sie auf den Seen, dann {crew|komm|komm|kommt} zurück und "
"{crew|hol|hol|holt} das Ersatzruder für sie."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hello! Yes, my oar broke, and I drift with one. Tell Tor to give you the spare one!"
msgstr ""
"Hallo! Ja, mein Ruder ist zerbrochen, und ich treibe mit einem herum. {crew|Sag|Sag|Sagt} Tor, er "
"soll {crew|dir|dir|euch} das Ersatzruder geben!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "She is well? Thank the gods. Here is the oar: bring it to her!"
msgstr ""
"Es geht ihr gut? Den Göttern sei Dank. Hier ist das Ruder: {crew|bring|bring|bringt} es ihr!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "My oar! Now I can row again. Here, take some fish: the freshest on the lakes."
msgstr ""
"Mein Ruder! Jetzt kann ich wieder rudern. Hier, {crew|nimm|nimm|nehmt} etwas Fisch: der frischeste"
" auf den Seen."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/044_ragnas_broken_oar/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every viking boat carried spare oars: a broken oar was common."
msgstr "Jedes Wikingerboot hatte Ersatzruder dabei: Ein Ruder zerbrach oft."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Torches for the Dark"
msgstr "Fackeln für die Dunkelheit"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The nights grow long. The guests of the autumn feast need light: bring me tar for torches, two "
"pots from Ekvik, and two crates of flax for the wicks."
msgstr ""
"Die Nächte werden lang. Die Gäste des Herbstfests brauchen Licht: {crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} mir "
"Teer für Fackeln, zwei Töpfe aus Ekvik, und zwei Kisten Flachs für die Dochte."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tar for torches? They burn bright and long."
msgstr "Teer für Fackeln? Die brennen hell und lange."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tar and flax: now my torches will light up the whole bay!"
msgstr "Teer und Flachs: Jetzt leuchten meine Fackeln die ganze Bucht aus!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking torches were sticks wrapped in flax or cloth, soaked in tar or fat."
msgstr ""
"Wikingerfackeln waren Stöcke, mit Flachs oder Stoff umwickelt und in Teer oder Fett getränkt."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Autumn Feast"
msgstr "Das Herbstfest"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The autumn feast is tomorrow! Knut's ale is ready, five barrels. Bring them from Lindtorp, and "
"bring three crates of fish for the soup too."
msgstr ""
"Morgen ist das Herbstfest! Knuts Bier ist fertig, fünf Fässer. {crew|Hol|Hol|Holt} sie aus "
"Lindtorp, und {crew|bring|bring|bringt} auch drei Kisten Fisch für die Suppe."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The ale! Now the fish."
msgstr "Das Bier! Jetzt den Fisch."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The biggest batch I ever brewed! Five barrels for Orm."
msgstr "So viel Bier habe ich noch nie gebraut! Fünf Fässer für Orm."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ale, soup, torches, Sten's flute and Hrafn's knives! Everybody is here. Dance with us!"
msgstr ""
"Bier, Suppe, Fackeln, Stens Flöte und Hrafns Messer! Alle sind da. {crew|Tanz|Tanz|Tanzt} mit uns!"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a barrel of ale|{count} barrels of ale}"
msgstr "{count|ein Fass Bier|{count} Fässer Bier}"

#. the thing '{count|a barrel of ale|{count} barrels of ale}' for {thing@acc} in the translations:
#. the accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the
#. same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a barrel of ale|{count} barrels of ale}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/046_the_autumn_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The autumn feast thanked the gods for the harvest, before the long winter."
msgstr "Mit dem Herbstfest dankte man den Göttern für die Ernte, vor dem langen Winter."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Tipsy Uncle"
msgstr "Der beschwipste Onkel"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Uncle Sven of Frosttorp sang and danced all night, and now he can't find his way home! He is very "
"merry and a little wobbly. Row him home to Arne, please."
msgstr ""
"Onkel Sven aus Frosttorp hat die ganze Nacht gesungen und getanzt, und jetzt findet er nicht mehr "
"nach Hause! Er ist sehr fröhlich und ein bisschen wackelig. {crew|Rudere|Rudere|Rudert} ihn bitte "
"heim zu Arne."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Uncle Sven! Singing all the way, I hear? Come in, sleep it off. Thank you, girls!"
msgstr ""
"Onkel Sven! Den ganzen Weg gesungen, höre ich? Komm herein und schlaf dich aus. Danke, {crew|mein "
"Junge|mein Mädchen|ihr zwei|ihr Mädchen}!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/047_the_tipsy_uncle/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Uncle Sven: Ho ho! Two little vikings with a boat! Let us sing on the way!"
msgstr ""
"Onkel Sven: Hoho! {crew|Ein kleiner Wikinger|Eine kleine Wikingerin|Zwei kleine Wikinger|Zwei "
"kleine Wikingerinnen} mit einem Boot! {crew|Lass|Lass|Lasst} uns unterwegs singen!"

