#. e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "the syrup"
msgstr "den Sirup"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/052_the_coughing_horse/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey helps a sore throat, for horses as for people."
msgstr "Honig hilft bei Halsweh, bei Pferden wie bei Menschen."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/053_the_lame_goat/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Lame Goat"
msgstr "Die lahme Ziege"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/053_the_lame_goat/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My best goat, Hedda, limps! A thorn, I think, but she won't let me look. Take her to Tova on "
"Laxön. She takes the room of a crate, and she butts!"
msgstr ""
"Meine beste Ziege, Hedda, hinkt! Ein Dorn, glaube ich, aber sie lässt mich nicht nachsehen. "
"{crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} sie zu Tova auf Laxön. Sie braucht so viel Platz wie eine Kiste, und sie"
" stößt mit den Hörnern!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/053_the_lame_goat/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hold her head, gently... There: a big thorn. Leave her with me tonight, with a herb wrap."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Halte|Halte|Haltet} ihren Kopf, ganz sanft ... So: ein großer Dorn. {crew|Lass|Lass|Lasst} "
"sie heute Nacht bei mir, mit einem Kräuterwickel."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/053_the_lame_goat/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hedda! She jumps like a kid again. Here, the best cheese I have."
msgstr "Hedda! Sie springt wieder wie ein Zicklein. Hier, der beste Käse, den ich habe."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/053_the_lame_goat/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "She walks well again. Take her home!"
msgstr "Sie läuft wieder gut. {crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} sie nach Hause!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/053_the_lame_goat/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hedda"
msgstr "Hedda"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/053_the_lame_goat/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hedda the goat"
msgstr "die Ziege Hedda"

#. the thing 'Hedda the goat' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the direct
#. object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain
#. translation
#: data/missions/053_the_lame_goat/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "Hedda the goat"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/053_the_lame_goat/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Goats climb anything: rocks, roofs, and sometimes boats."
msgstr "Ziegen klettern überall hinauf: auf Felsen, auf Dächer und manchmal auf Boote."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/054_barley_in_spring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Barley in Spring"
msgstr "Gerste im Frühling"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/054_barley_in_spring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The fields are dry: time to sow! Plant barley, and while it grows, sell two crates of eggs to Orm "
"in Hallvik to buy more seed."
msgstr ""
"Die Felder sind trocken: Zeit zum Säen! {crew|Pflanze|Pflanze|Pflanzt} Gerste, und während sie "
"wächst, {crew|verkaufe|verkaufe|verkauft} zwei Kisten Eier an Orm in Hallvik, um mehr Saatgut zu "
"kaufen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/054_barley_in_spring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The barley is sown. Now the sun and the rain do the work."
msgstr "Die Gerste ist gesät. Jetzt machen die Sonne und der Regen die Arbeit."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/054_barley_in_spring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Eggs! I make my famous egg cake. Here, good silver for good eggs."
msgstr "Eier! Ich backe meinen berühmten Eierkuchen. Hier, gutes Silber für gute Eier."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/054_barley_in_spring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Barley was the most important grain of the north: for bread, porridge and ale."
msgstr "Gerste war das wichtigste Getreide im Norden: für Brot, Brei und Bier."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Great Hold"
msgstr "Der große Laderaum"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Now we make your boat great! Ten planks from Frosttorp, three crates of tools, and 30 silver. Then"
" she takes two more crates. Ten planks are more than you can carry at once."
msgstr ""
"Jetzt machen wir {crew|dein|dein|euer} Boot groß! Zehn Planken aus Frosttorp, drei Kisten Werkzeug"
" und 30 Silber. Dann fasst es zwei Kisten mehr. Zehn Planken {crew|kannst du|kannst du|könnt ihr} "
"nicht auf einmal tragen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Planks again? Bjarne is building you a ship!"
msgstr "Schon wieder Planken? Bjarne baut {crew|dir|dir|euch} wohl ein Schiff!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Iron for the rivets. Now my wages."
msgstr "Eisen für die Nieten. Jetzt meinen Lohn."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Two more crates! And go and see Signe in Ekvik: she builds real ships, and my crates go with you "
"into any of them."
msgstr ""
"Zwei Kisten mehr! Und {crew|besuch|besuch|besucht} Signe in Ekvik: Sie baut richtige Schiffe, und "
"meine Kisten kommen in jedes davon mit."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A knarr, the cargo ship of the vikings, could carry the load of twenty boats."
msgstr "Eine Knorr, das Lastschiff der Wikinger, konnte so viel tragen wie zwanzig Boote."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/056_bjorns_salt_run/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bjørn's Salt Run"
msgstr "Bjørns Salzfahrt"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/056_bjorns_salt_run/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My boat leaks, and the fishers of Ekvik wait for salt! Take eight sacks for me from here to Ekvik."
" Your new hold is just right."
msgstr ""
"Mein Boot ist leck, und die Fischer in Ekvik warten auf Salz! {crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} für mich "
"acht Säcke von hier nach Ekvik. {crew|Dein|Dein|Euer} neuer Laderaum ist genau richtig."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/056_bjorns_salt_run/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bjørn's salt, brought by you? Then I pay you, not him. Ha!"
msgstr ""
"Bjørns Salz, und {crew|du bringst|du bringst|ihr bringt} es? Dann bezahle ich "
"{crew|dich|dich|euch}, nicht ihn. Ha!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/056_bjorns_salt_run/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Eight sacks of the best salt from the sea. Keep them dry!"
msgstr "Acht Säcke vom besten Salz aus dem Meer. {crew|Halte|Halte|Haltet} sie trocken!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/056_bjorns_salt_run/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Salt"
msgstr "Salz"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/056_bjorns_salt_run/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a sack of salt|{count} sacks of salt}"
msgstr "{count|ein Sack Salz|{count} Säcke Salz}"

#. the thing '{count|a sack of salt|{count} sacks of salt}' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the
#. accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same
#. as the plain translation
#: data/missions/056_bjorns_salt_run/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a sack of salt|{count} sacks of salt}"
msgstr "{count|einen Sack Salz|{count} Säcke Salz}"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/056_bjorns_salt_run/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Salt was boiled out of sea water in big pans, and traded far inland."
msgstr "Salz kochte man in großen Pfannen aus Meerwasser und handelte es weit ins Land hinein."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/057_eggs_for_the_spring_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Eggs for the Spring Feast"
msgstr "Eier für das Frühlingsfest"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/057_eggs_for_the_spring_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The spring feast! The children paint eggs and hide them in the grass. I need six crates of eggs. "
"Your hens are busy, I hope!"
msgstr ""
"Das Frühlingsfest! Die Kinder bemalen Eier und verstecken sie im Gras. Ich brauche sechs Kisten "
"Eier. Hoffentlich sind {crew|deine|deine|eure} Hühner fleißig!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/057_eggs_for_the_spring_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ivar and Märta paint them red and yellow already. Come and help us hide them!"
msgstr ""
"Ivar und Märta malen sie schon rot und gelb an. {crew|Komm|Komm|Kommt} und {crew|hilf|hilf|helft} "
"uns beim Verstecken!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/057_eggs_for_the_spring_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Eggs were a sign of spring and new life long before the Christian Easter."
msgstr ""
"Eier waren schon lange vor dem christlichen Ostern ein Zeichen für den Frühling und neues Leben."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
