msgid "The Cracked Kiln"
msgstr "Der gesprungene Brennofen"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/062_the_cracked_kiln/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My kiln cracked in the frost! To build a new one I need six baskets of clay from Ekvik and three "
"sacks of charcoal from Grim to fire it."
msgstr ""
"Mein Brennofen ist im Frost gesprungen! Um einen neuen zu bauen, brauche ich sechs Körbe Ton aus "
"Ekvik und drei Säcke Holzkohle von Grim zum Brennen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/062_the_cracked_kiln/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Clay again? Dagny must be building a castle!"
msgstr "Schon wieder Ton? Dagny baut wohl eine Burg!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/062_the_cracked_kiln/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The new kiln glows! My first pots from it are for you."
msgstr "Der neue Ofen glüht! Meine ersten Töpfe daraus sind für {crew|dich|dich|euch}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/062_the_cracked_kiln/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A potter's kiln is a small oven of clay, heated so hot that the pots glow."
msgstr "Der Brennofen einer Töpferin ist ein kleiner Ofen aus Ton, so heiß, dass die Töpfe glühen."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/063_hay_for_alberga/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hay for Ålberga"
msgstr "Heu für Ålberga"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/063_hay_for_alberga/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"So many lambs this spring! The ewes eat and eat, and my hay is gone. Bring me eight crates of hay "
"within two days."
msgstr ""
"So viele Lämmer in diesem Frühling! Die Mutterschafe fressen und fressen, und mein Heu ist alle. "
"{crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} mir acht Kisten Heu innerhalb von zwei Tagen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/063_hay_for_alberga/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Eight crates! The ewes munch, and the lambs jump around. Take a fleece of the softest wool."
msgstr ""
"Acht Kisten! Die Mutterschafe mampfen, und die Lämmer springen herum. {crew|Nimm|Nimm|Nehmt} ein "
"Vlies von der weichsten Wolle."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/063_hay_for_alberga/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A sheep eats about two kilograms of hay a day."
msgstr "Ein Schaf frisst etwa zwei Kilo Heu am Tag."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/064_the_ferrymans_last_trip/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Ferryman's Last Trip"
msgstr "Die letzte Fahrt des Fährmanns"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/064_the_ferrymans_last_trip/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Old Halvard says his bones are too old for the oars. He wants to live with his daughter in Solby. "
"Will you row him there? He has stories for the whole way."
msgstr ""
"Der alte Halvard sagt, seine Knochen sind zu alt für die Ruder. Er will bei seiner Tochter in "
"Solby wohnen. {crew|Ruderst du|Ruderst du|Rudert ihr} ihn hin? Er hat Geschichten für den ganzen "
"Weg."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/064_the_ferrymans_last_trip/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Father! Come in, your chair by the fire is ready. Thank you for bringing him."
msgstr ""
"Vater! Komm herein, dein Stuhl am Feuer ist bereit. Danke, dass {crew|du ihn gebracht hast|du ihn "
"gebracht hast|ihr ihn gebracht habt}."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/064_the_ferrymans_last_trip/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Old Halvard: Two young skippers for an old ferryman! Did I ever tell you about the sea serpent?"
msgstr ""
"Der alte Halvard: {crew|Ein junger Schiffer|Eine junge Schifferin|Zwei junge Schiffer|Zwei junge "
"Schifferinnen} für einen alten Fährmann! Habe ich {crew|dir|dir|euch} schon von der Seeschlange "
"erzählt?"

