#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/069_fish_for_the_hunters/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Fish for the Hunters"
msgstr "Fisch für die Jäger"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/069_fish_for_the_hunters/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My hunters go north for the whole summer. They need dried fish: six crates. Bring them within "
"three days, before they leave."
msgstr ""
"Meine Jäger ziehen für den ganzen Sommer nach Norden. Sie brauchen Trockenfisch: sechs Kisten. "
"{crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} sie innerhalb von drei Tagen, bevor sie aufbrechen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/069_fish_for_the_hunters/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Six crates! The hunters say: this fish tastes better than the bear meat. Ha! Here is your silver."
msgstr ""
"Sechs Kisten! Die Jäger sagen: Dieser Fisch schmeckt besser als Bärenfleisch. Ha! Hier ist "
"{crew|dein|dein|euer} Silber."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/069_fish_for_the_hunters/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Dried fish kept for years, and was the bread of the travellers."
msgstr "Trockenfisch hielt sich jahrelang und war das Brot der Reisenden."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/070_the_boat_procession/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Boat Procession"
msgstr "Die Bootsparade"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/070_the_boat_procession/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Midsummer again! This year, all the boats row in a line with torches. Bring three crates of mead, "
"and four torches from Orm in Hallvik: your boat leads the line!"
msgstr ""
"Wieder Mittsommer! Dieses Jahr rudern alle Boote mit Fackeln in einer Reihe. "
"{crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} drei Kisten Met und vier Fackeln von Orm in Hallvik: "
"{crew|Dein|Dein|Euer} Boot fährt vorneweg!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/070_the_boat_procession/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Mead for after the procession. Now the torches."
msgstr "Met für nach der Parade. Jetzt die Fackeln."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/070_the_boat_procession/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "My best tar torches, from the ones you helped me make!"
msgstr ""
"Meine besten Teerfackeln – die, bei denen {crew|du mir geholfen hast|du mir geholfen hast|ihr mir "
"geholfen habt}!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/070_the_boat_procession/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Twenty boats in a line, and you in front, with the dragon head! The torches shine on the water. "
"The most beautiful night of the year."
msgstr ""
"Zwanzig Boote in einer Reihe, und {crew|du|du|ihr} vorneweg, mit dem Drachenkopf! Die Fackeln "
"leuchten auf dem Wasser. Die schönste Nacht des Jahres."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/070_the_boat_procession/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Torch"
msgstr "Fackel"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
