#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/071_the_sunny_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The land of a family passed from mother and father to the children; women could own land too."
msgstr ""
"Das Land einer Familie ging von Mutter und Vater an die Kinder; auch Frauen konnten Land besitzen."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/072_a_flock_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Flock of Our Own"
msgstr "Eine eigene Herde"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/072_a_flock_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The sunny hill has the best grass. Let us have a real flock: five sheep! Buy them at the market or"
" from Sten's herders."
msgstr ""
"Auf dem sonnigen Hügel wächst das beste Gras. Wir wollen eine richtige Herde haben: fünf Schafe! "
"{crew|Kauf|Kauf|Kauft} sie auf dem Markt oder bei Stens Hirten."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/072_a_flock_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Five sheep on the hill, like white clouds. We will have wool for the whole family!"
msgstr "Fünf Schafe auf dem Hügel, wie weiße Wolken. Wir werden Wolle für die ganze Familie haben!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/072_a_flock_of_our_own/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sheep gave wool, milk, meat and skins; nothing was wasted."
msgstr "Schafe gaben Wolle, Milch, Fleisch und Felle; nichts wurde verschwendet."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/073_the_bear_comes_back/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Bear Comes Back"
msgstr "Der Bär kommt zurück"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/073_the_bear_comes_back/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Honey is missing again! But this time, the paw prints are BIG. Ask Inga the messenger, she rows "
"past the woods every day."
msgstr ""
"Schon wieder fehlt Honig! Aber diesmal sind die Pfotenabdrücke GROSS. {crew|Frag|Frag|Fragt} Botin"
" Inga, sie rudert jeden Tag am Wald vorbei."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/073_the_bear_comes_back/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A young bear by the woods of Hjortingsala, with a white spot on his chest. The cub you carried, "
"all grown up!"
msgstr ""
"Ein junger Bär am Wald von Hjortingsala, mit einem weißen Fleck auf der Brust. Das Bärenjunge, das"
" {crew|du getragen hast|du getragen hast|ihr getragen habt}, ganz erwachsen!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/073_the_bear_comes_back/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I put the pots by the old oak. Look! He comes out of the bushes and sniffs. He remembers you!"
msgstr ""
"Ich stelle die Töpfe an die alte Eiche. {crew|Schau|Schau|Schaut}! Er kommt aus den Büschen und "
"schnuppert. Er erinnert sich an {crew|dich|dich|euch}!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/073_the_bear_comes_back/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Then he gets honey of his own, far from my hives. Take him two pots."
msgstr ""
"Dann bekommt er eigenen Honig, weit weg von meinen Bienenstöcken. {crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} ihm "
"zwei Töpfe."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
