#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/073_the_bear_comes_back/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Brown bears live alone in the woods, eat berries, roots, fish and, yes, honey."
msgstr "Braunbären leben allein im Wald und fressen Beeren, Wurzeln, Fisch und, ja, Honig."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/074_a_striped_sail/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Striped Sail"
msgstr "Ein gestreiftes Segel"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/074_a_striped_sail/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Your boat has a dragon head, but no sail. I will weave you a little one, with red and white "
"stripes. Bring me six crates of wool, and give me two nights."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Dein|Dein|Euer} Boot hat einen Drachenkopf, aber kein Segel. Ich webe {crew|dir|dir|euch} "
"ein kleines, mit roten und weißen Streifen. {crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} mir sechs Kisten Wolle, und "
"{crew|gib|gib|gebt} mir zwei Nächte Zeit."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/074_a_striped_sail/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now the looms clatter. Come back in two days!"
msgstr "Jetzt klappern die Webstühle. {crew|Komm|Komm|Kommt} in zwei Tagen wieder!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/074_a_striped_sail/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Red and white stripes, like the great ships! It is small, but on a windy day it helps your arms."
msgstr ""
"Rote und weiße Streifen, wie bei den großen Schiffen! Es ist klein, aber an einem windigen Tag "
"hilft es {crew|deinen|deinen|euren} Armen."

#. a gift for a task: 'You get ...'
#: data/missions/074_a_striped_sail/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "a striped sail"
msgstr "ein gestreiftes Segel"

#. the thing 'a striped sail' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the direct
#. object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain
#. translation
#: data/missions/074_a_striped_sail/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "a striped sail"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/074_a_striped_sail/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A big viking sail took a weaver years; it was worth as much as the ship."
msgstr ""
"Für ein großes Wikingersegel brauchte eine Weberin Jahre; es war so viel wert wie das Schiff."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/075_the_widest_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Widest Hold"
msgstr "Der breiteste Laderaum"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/075_the_widest_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Last time, I promise! Six oak branches from Frosttorp, four boxes of rivets from Hrafn, and 40 "
"silver: your hold takes two more crates, whatever ship you row."
msgstr ""
"Zum letzten Mal, versprochen! Sechs Eichenäste aus Frosttorp, vier Schachteln Nieten von Hrafn und"
" 40 Silber: Dann fasst {crew|dein|dein|euer} Laderaum zwei Kisten mehr, egal welches Schiff "
"{crew|du ruderst|du ruderst|ihr rudert}."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/075_the_widest_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Rivets for Bjarne? He must love you two."
msgstr "Nieten für Bjarne? Er hat {crew|dich|dich|euch zwei} wohl sehr gern."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/075_the_widest_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Two more crates! Now your hold is the widest on the lakes. Now go and trade like the big ships."
msgstr ""
"Zwei Kisten mehr! Jetzt ist {crew|dein|dein|euer} Laderaum der breiteste auf den Seen. Jetzt "
"{crew|geh|geh|geht} und {crew|handle|handle|handelt} wie die großen Schiffe."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/075_the_widest_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Rivets"
msgstr "Nieten"

