#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ale for Two Inns"
msgstr "Bier für zwei Gasthäuser"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Both inns ran dry at the same time! Six barrels for Gudrun in Vargvik and six for Orm in Hallvik. "
"With twelve crates of room, you can do it in one trip!"
msgstr ""
"Beide Gasthäuser haben gleichzeitig kein Bier mehr! Sechs Fässer für Gudrun in Vargvik und sechs "
"für Orm in Hallvik. Mit zwölf Kisten Platz {crew|schaffst du|schaffst du|schafft ihr} das in einer"
" Fahrt!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ale! The guests cheer. Thank you!"
msgstr "Bier! Die Gäste jubeln. Danke!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "At last! I thought I must serve water. Here, silver for you and for Knut."
msgstr ""
"Endlich! Ich dachte schon, ich muss Wasser ausschenken. Hier, Silber für {crew|dich|dich|euch} und"
" für Knut."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Everybody drank weak ale every day: it was safer than water from the lake."
msgstr "Alle tranken jeden Tag dünnes Bier: Das war sicherer als Wasser aus dem See."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/078_the_sleepy_hens/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Sleepy Hens"
msgstr "Die müden Hühner"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/078_the_sleepy_hens/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Our hens sit sleepy in the corner and lay no eggs. You are healers now: what do they need? Ask "
"Tova, and bring it."
msgstr ""
"Unsere Hühner sitzen müde in der Ecke und legen keine Eier. {crew|Du bist|Du bist|Ihr seid} jetzt "
"{crew|Heiler|Heilerin|Heiler|Heilerinnen}: Was brauchen sie? {crew|Frag|Frag|Fragt} Tova, und "
"{crew|bring|bring|bringt} es mit."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/078_the_sleepy_hens/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Sleepy hens? Lice, I bet. Dust baths with wood ash and a bit of garlic in the water. Here, take "
"garlic."
msgstr ""
"Müde Hühner? Bestimmt Läuse. Staubbäder mit Holzasche und ein bisschen Knoblauch ins Wasser. Hier,"
" {crew|nimm|nimm|nehmt} Knoblauch."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/078_the_sleepy_hens/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Garlic water, ash baths, fresh grain... Cluck! An egg! You are real healers."
msgstr ""
"Knoblauchwasser, Aschebäder, frisches Korn ... Gack! Ein Ei! {crew|Du bist ein echter Heiler|Du "
"bist eine echte Heilerin|Ihr seid echte Heiler|Ihr seid echte Heilerinnen}."

