#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/081_the_healers_round/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Healers looked, listened and touched: they had no tools but their hands and their herbs."
msgstr ""
"Die Heiler schauten, hörten zu und tasteten: Sie hatten kein Werkzeug außer ihren Händen und ihren"
" Kräutern."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Colt in the Mud"
msgstr "Das Fohlen im Schlamm"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Silke's colt ran into the bog and is stuck to his belly! I need a long rope: Tor in Stormvik has "
"the longest. Hurry, he is scared!"
msgstr ""
"Silkes Hengstfohlen ist ins Moor gelaufen und steckt bis zum Bauch fest! Ich brauche ein langes "
"Seil: Tor in Stormvik hat das längste. Schnell, es hat Angst!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Rope around him, gently, everybody pull... Slurp! He is out! Muddy, but well. You saved him."
msgstr ""
"Das Seil um das Fohlen, ganz sanft, alle ziehen ... Schlurp! Es ist draußen! Schlammig, aber "
"gesund. {crew|Du hast|Du hast|Ihr habt} es gerettet."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "My longest rope! Take it, quick!"
msgstr "Mein längstes Seil! {crew|Nimm|Nimm|Nehmt} es, schnell!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Rope"
msgstr "Seil"

