#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/082_the_colt_in_the_mud/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A horse stuck in mud must be pulled out slowly, or it hurts its legs."
msgstr ""
"Ein Pferd, das im Schlamm steckt, muss man langsam herausziehen, sonst verletzt es sich die Beine."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Grain for the North"
msgstr "Getreide für den Norden"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My hunters send news: the summer in the north was cold, and their families have no grain. My ship "
"leaves in three days: fill it with twelve crates!"
msgstr ""
"Meine Jäger schicken Nachricht: Der Sommer im Norden war kalt, und ihre Familien haben kein "
"Getreide. Mein Schiff fährt in drei Tagen ab: {crew|Füll|Füll|Füllt} es mit zwölf Kisten!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Twelve crates! Nobody in the north goes hungry this winter. The whole valley thanks you."
msgstr ""
"Zwölf Kisten! Im Norden muss diesen Winter niemand hungern. Das ganze Tal dankt "
"{crew|dir|dir|euch}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/083_grain_for_the_north/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "When the harvest failed, the farms helped each other: next year, it might be them."
msgstr ""
"Wenn die Ernte schlecht war, halfen sich die Höfe gegenseitig: Nächstes Jahr konnte es sie selbst "
"treffen."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Wool Fair"
msgstr "Der Wollmarkt"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The wool fair! Traders come from the Long Lake to buy. Bring me eight crates of wool, the more the"
" better, and the fair is a success."
msgstr ""
"Der Wollmarkt! Händler kommen vom Langen See, um zu kaufen. {crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} mir acht "
"Kisten Wolle, je mehr, desto besser, dann wird der Markt ein Erfolg."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Eight crates! The traders from the Long Lake ask: who are these girls? I say: the best traders of "
"the Home Lakes."
msgstr ""
"Acht Kisten! Die Händler vom Langen See fragen: Wer {crew|ist dieser Junge|ist dieses Mädchen|sind"
" diese zwei|sind diese Mädchen}? Ich sage: {crew|der beste Händler|die beste Händlerin|die besten "
"Händler|die besten Händlerinnen} der Heimatseen."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/084_the_wool_fair/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Wool was so important that some sagas tell of whole ships full of it."
msgstr "Wolle war so wichtig, dass manche Sagas von ganzen Schiffen voller Wolle erzählen."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Goats on the Island"
msgstr "Die Ziegen auf der Insel"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My four goats swam to Bergö! They eat Dagny's flowers, and she is cross. Bring them back before "
"they eat her kiln too!"
msgstr ""
"Meine vier Ziegen sind nach Bergö geschwommen! Sie fressen Dagnys Blumen, und sie ist böse. "
"{crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} sie zurück, bevor sie auch noch ihren Brennofen fressen!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "My naughty goats! Tomorrow I build a higher fence. Here, my best cheese."
msgstr "Meine frechen Ziegen! Morgen baue ich einen höheren Zaun. Hier, mein bester Käse."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take them, take them! They ate my flowers and a basket and a shoe!"
msgstr ""
"{crew|Nimm|Nimm|Nehmt} sie mit, {crew|nimm|nimm|nehmt} sie mit! Sie haben meine Blumen gefressen "
"und einen Korb und einen Schuh!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/085_the_goats_on_the_island/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Goats are good swimmers when they must be, and they eat nearly anything."
msgstr "Ziegen schwimmen gut, wenn sie müssen, und sie fressen fast alles."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "News for Everybody"
msgstr "Neuigkeiten für alle"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Big news: a ship from the Long Lake will come, and the way between the lakes opens! Tell the "
"smith, the fishers of Stormvik and Orm in Hallvik. I tell the rest."
msgstr ""
"Große Neuigkeiten: Ein Schiff vom Langen See kommt, und der Weg zwischen den Seen öffnet sich! "
"{crew|Sag|Sag|Sagt} es dem Schmied, den Fischern von Stormvik und Orm in Hallvik. Den anderen sage"
" ich es."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A ship from the Long Lake? They will want my iron!"
msgstr "Ein Schiff vom Langen See? Die wollen bestimmt mein Eisen!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "New lakes, new fish! Thank you for telling us."
msgstr ""
"Neue Seen, neue Fische! Danke, dass {crew|du es uns erzählst|du es uns erzählst|ihr es uns "
"erzählt}."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Guests from far away! I must brew more. Thank you, girls!"
msgstr ""
"Gäste von weit her! Ich muss mehr brauen. Danke, {crew|mein Junge|mein Mädchen|ihr zwei|ihr "
"Mädchen}!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/086_news_for_everybody/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The lakes of the north were joined by rivers and portages, where boats were dragged over land."
msgstr ""
"Die Seen im Norden waren durch Flüsse und Tragestellen verbunden, wo man die Boote über Land zog."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Cow for Grim"
msgstr "Eine Kuh für Grim"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I am old, and I would like fresh milk every morning. Bring me a cow from the horse farm. The swans"
" will be jealous!"
msgstr ""
"Ich bin alt, und ich hätte gern jeden Morgen frische Milch. {crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} mir eine Kuh"
" vom Pferdehof. Da werden die Schwäne neidisch!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A cow! I call her Swan, ha. Here, for your trouble, and for all the years you visited an old man."
msgstr ""
"Eine Kuh! Ich nenne sie Schwan, ha. Hier, für {crew|deine|deine|eure} Mühe, und für all die Jahre,"
" in denen {crew|du einen alten Mann besucht hast|du einen alten Mann besucht hast|ihr einen alten "
"Mann besucht habt}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/087_a_cow_for_grim/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A good cow gave milk for ten years or more, and was part of the family."
msgstr "Eine gute Kuh gab zehn Jahre oder länger Milch und gehörte zur Familie."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flowers on the Hill"
msgstr "Blumen auf dem Hügel"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Plant flowers on the sunny hill! When they bloom, bring three crates to Gudrun's inn: she wants "
"the inn to smell like summer."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Pflanze|Pflanze|Pflanzt} Blumen auf dem sonnigen Hügel! Wenn sie blühen, "
"{crew|bring|bring|bringt} drei Kisten zu Gudruns Gasthaus: Sie möchte, dass das Gasthaus nach "
"Sommer duftet."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flower seeds in the earth. In two days, they bloom."
msgstr "Blumensamen in der Erde. In zwei Tagen blühen sie."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Flowers on every table! The guests smile. Here is your silver, and a cup of milk for each of you."
msgstr ""
"Blumen auf jedem Tisch! Die Gäste lächeln. Hier ist {crew|dein|dein|euer} Silber, und {crew|ein "
"Becher Milch für dich|ein Becher Milch für dich|für jeden von euch ein Becher Milch}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/088_flowers_on_the_hill/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Vikings wove flowers into wreaths and crowns for feasts and weddings."
msgstr "Die Wikinger flochten Blumen zu Kränzen und Kronen für Feste und Hochzeiten."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Pottery Market"
msgstr "Der Töpfermarkt"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The new kiln makes so many pots! Bring ten crates to the market in Kråkhamn. Ten crates: only your"
" big boat can do it."
msgstr ""
"Der neue Brennofen macht so viele Töpfe! {crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} zehn Kisten zum Markt in "
"Kråkhamn. Zehn Kisten: Das schafft nur {crew|dein|dein|euer} großes Boot."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ten crates of Dagny's pots, and not one broken! The best rowing of the lakes."
msgstr "Zehn Kisten mit Dagnys Töpfen, und kein einziger zerbrochen! Das beste Rudern auf den Seen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pack them in straw: pots do not like to bump!"
msgstr "{crew|Pack|Pack|Packt} sie in Stroh: Töpfe mögen kein Gerumpel!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pots"
msgstr "Töpfe"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a crate of pots|{count} crates of pots}"
msgstr "{count|eine Kiste Töpfe|{count} Kisten Töpfe}"

#. the thing '{count|a crate of pots|{count} crates of pots}' for {thing@acc} in the translations:
#. the accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the
#. same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a crate of pots|{count} crates of pots}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/089_the_pottery_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Clay pots were carried packed in straw, so that they did not break."
msgstr "Tontöpfe wurden in Stroh verpackt transportiert, damit sie nicht zerbrachen."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Gudrun's Ring"
msgstr "Gudruns Ring"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My mother's ring! It slipped from my finger into the lake, by the jetty. Gone forever... unless a "
"fisher's net caught it? Ask Ragna."
msgstr ""
"Der Ring meiner Mutter! Er ist mir am Steg vom Finger in den See gerutscht. Für immer weg ... "
"außer, das Netz eines Fischers hat ihn gefangen? {crew|Frag|Frag|Fragt} Ragna."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A ring? Wait... Tor found something shiny in our net yesterday! Ask him in Stormvik."
msgstr ""
"Ein Ring? Warte ... Tor hat gestern etwas Glänzendes in unserem Netz gefunden! "
"{crew|Frag|Frag|Fragt} ihn in Stormvik."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My mother's ring! Back from the lake! I can not thank you enough. Every meal at my inn is free for"
" you."
msgstr ""
"Der Ring meiner Mutter! Zurück aus dem See! Ich kann {crew|dir|dir|euch} gar nicht genug danken. "
"Jedes Essen in meinem Gasthaus ist für {crew|dich|dich|euch} umsonst."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "This? Silver with a little red stone. I thought it was a fish's treasure!"
msgstr "Das hier? Silber mit einem kleinen roten Stein. Ich dachte, das ist ein Fischschatz!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ring"
msgstr "Ring"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "the ring"
msgstr "der Ring"

#. the thing 'the ring' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the direct object),
#. e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "the ring"
msgstr "den Ring"

#. a gift for a task: 'You get ...'
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "free meals at the inn of Vargvik"
msgstr "freies Essen im Gasthaus von Vargvik"

#. the thing 'free meals at the inn of Vargvik' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative
#. (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the
#. plain translation
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "free meals at the inn of Vargvik"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Vikings sometimes gave silver to the lakes on purpose, as gifts to the gods."
msgstr "Die Wikinger gaben den Seen manchmal absichtlich Silber, als Geschenk an die Götter."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Edge of the Forest"
msgstr "Der Waldrand"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Kol and Ingrid want sheep for their new home. Bring them two sheep, and I give you the strip of "
"land by the forest, next to your farm. A fair trade!"
msgstr ""
"Kol und Ingrid wollen Schafe für ihr neues Zuhause. {crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} ihnen zwei Schafe, "
"dann gebe ich {crew|dir|dir|euch} den Streifen Land am Wald, gleich neben "
"{crew|deinem|deinem|eurem} Hof. Ein fairer Tausch!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Two sheep for the young ones! Ingrid already knits. The forest edge is yours: good wood and two "
"fields."
msgstr ""
"Zwei Schafe für die jungen Leute! Ingrid strickt schon. Der Waldrand gehört {crew|dir|dir|euch}: "
"gutes Holz und zwei Felder."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Land was traded for animals, silver or work: there were no banks."
msgstr "Land tauschte man gegen Tiere, Silber oder Arbeit: Es gab keine Banken."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Longhouse Grows"
msgstr "Das Langhaus wächst"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With so many animals and friends, our house is too small! Bring twelve logs from Frosttorp, two "
"crates of tools and two pots of tar, and we make it longer."
msgstr ""
"Mit so vielen Tieren und Freunden ist unser Haus zu klein! {crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} zwölf "
"Baumstämme aus Frosttorp, zwei Kisten Werkzeug und zwei Töpfe Teer, dann machen wir es länger."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Twelve logs! Fill that big hold of yours."
msgstr "Zwölf Baumstämme! {crew|Füll|Füll|Füllt} {crew|deinen|deinen|euren} großen Laderaum."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Axes and nails. Now the tar for the roof."
msgstr "Äxte und Nägel. Jetzt den Teer für das Dach."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hammering all night with the neighbours... Our longhouse is twice as long! Room for a feast."
msgstr ""
"Die ganze Nacht mit den Nachbarn gehämmert ... Unser Langhaus ist doppelt so lang! Platz für ein "
"Fest."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A longhouse could be made longer by adding a piece at the end, like a train."
msgstr ""
"Ein Langhaus konnte man länger machen, indem man am Ende ein Stück anbaute, wie bei einem Zug."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Green Valley"
msgstr "Das grüne Tal"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You helped my valley all year. The green valley behind your farm has no owner: bring me two crates"
" of cloth and two of honey for the gods' feast, and it is yours."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Du hast|Du hast|Ihr habt} meinem Tal das ganze Jahr geholfen. Das grüne Tal hinter "
"{crew|deinem|deinem|eurem} Hof hat keinen Besitzer: {crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} mir zwei Kisten "
"Stoff und zwei Kisten Honig für das Götterfest, dann gehört es {crew|dir|dir|euch}."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cloth for the hall. Now the honey."
msgstr "Stoff für die Halle. Jetzt den Honig."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Father says it at the Thing, in front of everybody: the green valley belongs to Ylva and Sigrid!"
msgstr "Vater verkündet es auf dem Thing, vor allen: Das grüne Tal gehört Ylva und Sigrid!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "At the Thing, the meeting of the free people, land and laws were decided."
msgstr "Auf dem Thing, der Versammlung der freien Leute, entschied man über Land und Gesetze."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bees for the Valley"
msgstr "Bienen für das Tal"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The valley is full of clover and heather. Bees would love it! Have three beehives on the farm, and"
" we will have honey all year."
msgstr ""
"Das Tal ist voller Klee und Heidekraut. Das würde den Bienen gefallen! {crew|Halte|Halte|Haltet} "
"drei Bienenstöcke auf dem Hof, dann haben wir das ganze Jahr Honig."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hum, hum, hum! Three hives in the valley. Honey for us, and for mead."
msgstr "Summ, summ, summ! Drei Bienenstöcke im Tal. Honig für uns und für den Met."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Heather honey is dark and strong; clover honey is light and mild."
msgstr "Heidehonig ist dunkel und kräftig; Kleehonig ist hell und mild."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Apples for the Market"
msgstr "Äpfel für den Markt"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Thanks to the bees, my trees are full of apples! Twelve baskets for the market in Kråkhamn. Only "
"your boat can take them all at once."
msgstr ""
"Dank der Bienen hängen meine Bäume voller Äpfel! Zwölf Körbe für den Markt in Kråkhamn. Nur "
"{crew|dein|dein|euer} Boot kann sie alle auf einmal tragen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Twelve baskets of apples! The whole market smells of autumn."
msgstr "Zwölf Körbe Äpfel! Der ganze Markt duftet nach Herbst."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Red and green and yellow. Take one for the trip!"
msgstr "Rot und grün und gelb. {crew|Nimm|Nimm|Nehmt} einen für unterwegs!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Apples"
msgstr "Äpfel"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a basket of apples|{count} baskets of apples}"
msgstr "{count|ein Korb Äpfel|{count} Körbe Äpfel}"

#. the thing '{count|a basket of apples|{count} baskets of apples}' for {thing@acc} in the
#. translations: the accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty
#. if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a basket of apples|{count} baskets of apples}"
msgstr "{count|einen Korb Äpfel|{count} Körbe Äpfel}"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The vikings ate wild apples, dried for the winter."
msgstr "Die Wikinger aßen wilde Äpfel, getrocknet für den Winter."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/096_the_winter_stores/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Winter Stores"
msgstr "Die Wintervorräte"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/096_the_winter_stores/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Autumn again! Before the lakes freeze, fill the store: ten crates of hay and six of grain, within "
"three days. You know how by now!"
msgstr ""
"Wieder Herbst! Bevor die Seen zufrieren, {crew|füll|füll|füllt} das Lager: zehn Kisten Heu und "
"sechs Kisten Getreide, innerhalb von drei Tagen. {crew|Du weißt|Du weißt|Ihr wisst} inzwischen, "
"wie das geht!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/096_the_winter_stores/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hay for all our animals. Now the grain."
msgstr "Heu für alle unsere Tiere. Jetzt das Getreide."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/096_the_winter_stores/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The store is full to the roof! Not one animal will be hungry this winter."
msgstr "Das Lager ist bis unters Dach voll! Kein einziges Tier wird diesen Winter hungern."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/096_the_winter_stores/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Autumn was the busiest time: everything for the long winter had to be in."
msgstr "Der Herbst war die geschäftigste Zeit: Alles für den langen Winter musste unter Dach sein."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/097_fish_for_every_farm/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Fish for Every Farm"
msgstr "Fisch für jeden Hof"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/097_fish_for_every_farm/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Our best catch ever! Bring three bundles of dried fish to each farm: Frosttorp, Solby and "
"Svanetorp. A gift from Stormvik, for the winter."
msgstr ""
"Unser bester Fang aller Zeiten! {crew|Bring|Bring|Bringt} jedem Hof drei Bündel Trockenfisch: "
"Frosttorp, Solby und Svanetorp. Ein Geschenk aus Stormvik, für den Winter."

